# Intentionally empty of ownership rules. Read the history before adding one.
#
# This file used to carry `/.github/ @Vinylfigure`, which — combined with
# "Require review from Code Owners" on `main` — made every machinery change
# unmergeable by the only person who writes them. GitHub does not let anyone
# approve their own pull request, so a solo-maintained repository that names
# its sole maintainer as the code owner of a path has locked that path shut.
# PR #30 sat blocked on exactly this: all checks green, no reviewer possible.
#
# The control the rule was reaching for still exists, and is satisfiable:
# `.github/workflows/gate-integrity.yml` fails any PR that touches
# `.github/workflows/**`, deletes tests, or adds skipped tests, unless the PR
# carries the `machinery-change` label. That label is an explicit, deliberate,
# operator-visible act recorded on the PR — the same signal a code-owner
# review was meant to give, minus the deadlock.
#
# Restore an ownership rule when there is a second human who can approve:
#
#   /.github/ @some-team-with-more-than-one-member
#
# A rule naming only the sole maintainer is not a safeguard; it is an outage.
